      ],
      "impact": "If populated as 1 Ω, the series resistor provides almost no current limiting or protection for the PWM2 signal, potentially damaging the M5Stack GPIO or servo and altering signal integrity. If the BOM uses the LCSC part C21190 (1 kΩ), the board may still be correct, but the design file value is wrong.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain one anomaly: R4 is specified as 1 Ω instead of the intended 1 kΩ series resistor for the PWM2 servo signal, while all other components match the specification."
